  {
   "tool": {
    "driver": {
     "name": "antigravity",
     "version": "1.1.26",
     "rules": [
      {
       "id": "PRREV-AGY",
       "name": "cross-vendor review (advisory)"
      },
      {
       "id": "PRREV-AGY-PRIOR",
       "name": "cross-vendor review, earlier runs on this PR (advisory)"
      }
     ]
    }
   },
   "results": [
    {
     "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY",
     "level": "note",
     "message": {
      "text": "(1) Deadlock analysis is correct. GpuDevice::new holds DEVICE_INIT_LOCK while waiting on shared_instance(), and is_available_async enters shared_instance() without holding DEVICE_INIT_LOCK, creating the ABBA cycle. Removing the lock is safe because OnceLock ensures wgpu::Instance is created exactly once, serializing the ICD enumeration. There are no other wgpu::Instance creation paths outside shared_instance()."
     },
     "locations": [
      {
       "physicalLocation": {
        "artifactLocation": {
         "uri": "crates/aprender-compute/src/backends/gpu/device/mod.rs"
        },
        "region": {
         "startLine": 80
        }
       }
      }
     ],
     "properties": {
      "grounding": "measured",
      "precision_class": "advisory",
      "failure_scenario": "none stated",
      "source": "agy gemini-3.1-pro-high on 2f36db3e5: ",
      "excerpt": "",
      "excerpt_sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
      "disposition": "confirmation; re-verified by the primary: fix 2 passed, mutant (mutex restored) FAILED with the probe child exit 101, fix again 2 passed",
      "agy_id": "F1",
      "baselineState": "new"
     }
    },
    {
     "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY",
     "level": "note",
     "message": {
      "text": "(2) The test correctly discriminates. It does not pass vacuously: when the mutex is restored, the inner probe blocks, rx.recv_timeout panics after 30s, the child exits with 101, and the parent test correctly fails due to the `status.success()` assert. The --exact path is correct for the crate layout (trueno). The 30s/90s timeout pair is sound and ensures failure is caught. The child is killed if it hangs, preventing leakage."
     },
     "locations": [
      {
       "physicalLocation": {
        "artifactLocation": {
         "uri": "crates/aprender-compute/src/backends/gpu/device/mod.rs"
        },
        "region": {
         "startLine": 601
        }
       }
      }
     ],
     "properties": {
      "grounding": "measured",
      "precision_class": "advisory",
      "failure_scenario": "none stated",
      "source": "agy gemini-3.1-pro-high on 2f36db3e5: ",
      "excerpt": "",
      "excerpt_sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
      "disposition": "confirmation; re-verified by the primary: fix 2 passed, mutant (mutex restored) FAILED with the probe child exit 101, fix again 2 passed",
      "agy_id": "F2",
      "baselineState": "new"
     }
    },
    {
     "ruleId": "PRREV-AGY",
     "level": "note",
     "message": {
      "text": "(3) No regression risk for wasm32 or non-gpu builds. The test is correctly cfg-gated (feature = \"gpu\", not(target_arch = \"wasm32\")). For wasm32, DEVICE_INIT_LOCK is never taken in `new()`, and its removal from `shared_instance()` just avoids taking a lock unnecessarily. Non-gpu builds are protected by top-level cfg feature gates."
     },
     "locations": [
      {
       "physicalLocation": {
